  "preview": null,
  "automatic_result_preview": true,
  "output_display": "auto",
  "help": "Siril 1.4.4. Generates an intensity profile plot between 2 points in each image in the sequence. After the mandatory first argument stating the sequence to process, the other arguments are the same as for the profile command. If processing a sequence and it is desired to have the current image number and total number of images displayed in the format \"My Sequence (1 / 5)\", the given title should end with () (e.g. \"My Sequence ()\" and the numbers will be populated automatically)\n\nUses fixed input references and writes only invocation-owned outputs. Optional argument values are sent only when their use_* control is true; zero is preserved.\n\n\n\nruntime is a JSON object. Supported keys: ini, settings, threads, memory_ratio, output_bits, compression, online, selection, findstar, photometry. Networking starts offline and must be enabled explicitly. Selection is omitted for the whole image or explicitly null to clear it; optional CLI arguments use separate use_* controls. Automatic complete-result calculation can target explicitly opted-in processing and analysis operations without an export node. Manual execution retains explicit export, stacking, or analysis endpoints. Only requested dependencies are executed. Saved output references identify complete checked files, never preview pixels. See reference/coverage.json and docs/usage.md.",
  "examples": [
